WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
 (soft piano music)

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:10.360
 In this video, we're going to actually download

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:15.080
 and install Python 3 from python.org on a Macintosh.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.960
 If your Macintosh for years has wonderfully come

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.120
 with Python 2, so if I type Python minus minus version,

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.580
 then if I type that, I see that I've got Python 2.0.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.740
 What we want to do is, in addition, install Python 3.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:35.560
 One of these days, Macintosh might upgrade

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.700
 their distributed version of Python 3,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.380
 but there's so many things inside Mac

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.740
 that depend on Python 2, I'm going to expect

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.820
 that it will always be named Python 3,

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:49.080
 which is what we're going to call it in a second.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.520
 So, here I am at the python.org downloads,

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.280
 and I'm going to download Python 3.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.820
 You click here, and I've actually got it sitting here

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:01.360
 in downloads already, because I always do that.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.100
 And so, I'm going to install this.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.880
 There is the installer.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.240
 I'm going to say continue, continue, continue.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.900
 Of course I agree, I read all that really fast,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.620
 and now I'm going to install it.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.540
 (soft piano music)

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:26.460
 Okay, so now, that means if I run a terminal,

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.280
 so this, of course, is start run terminal.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.500
 So, Python 2 is still there,

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.020
 but Python 3 is also now involved there,

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.020
 so we should have Python 3 installed.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.180
 So, we installed Python 3.6, and so there we go,

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.960
 and that's all it takes to install Python 3

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.900
 on the Macintosh.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.060
 So, let's write our first little Python program.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.140
 I'm going to, I like Adam,

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.740
 and so I've got this Adam editor, it's adam.io.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:05.140
 Right here, adam.io, download and install the Adam editor.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.620
 I like it because Adam works the same

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.820
 on both Windows, Mac, and Linux,

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.200
 and it has syntax highlighting,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.000
 and so I really like things like that.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.160
 So, I'm going to make myself a simple Python program.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.540
 Hello, world, like we always do.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.900
 Now, you'll notice that it's not syntax highlighting yet,

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.220
 but I'm going to do a file, save, oopsie daisy.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:34.760
 File, save as, and I'm going to go into my desktop,

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.180
 and I'm going to make a folder called py4e.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:43.820
 I'm just going to, let's call this hello.py.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:47.380
 Oh, crud.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.920
 Gotta rename it, rename it.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.140
 I ended up with two dots.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.320
 Hello.py, there we are.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.340
 And so now I'm here, and I'm in my home folder.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.040
 I can go in my desktop, and I can go into that new folder

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.260
 I made, Python for Everybody, and I can see the files.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.420
 Now, there are ways to run this,

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:12.740
 and I really want you to learn the terminal

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.100
 so that you really know what you're doing.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.140
 And so here we are, we are in the folder that has the Python,

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:21.300
 and then all we do to run it is we say python3 hello.py,

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.800
 and there we go, and of course, this is python3,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.500
 because I'm using parentheses there.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:32.160
 So, instead of double quotes, but python2 is still there,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.080
 and of course, if you just run python hello.py,

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.840
 it'll be a syntax error, or not.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.140
 Must be they added something.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.020
 (laughs)

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:45.020
 Yeah, because Python is still version,

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.320
 still version two, but apparently they allowed print

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.320
 in the latest version of python2, so away we go.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.840
 Okay, so again, thanks for watching.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.720
 I hope this was helpful to you to get python3 installed

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.300
 on your Macintosh.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.560
 (jazz music)

